  "assertions": [
    "the formal adapter remains frozen at max_concurrency one so a permanent failure can stop before any later position enters its callable",
    "the stop event is set after the frozen retry budget returns an infrastructure-error result and before the worker can invoke the next queued position",
    "queued positions are guarded before their task callable and skipped positions create no task-attempt or model-usage event",
    "the permanent failure result and every prior checkpoint remain in the upstream result while skipped futures are excluded from the returned population",
    "the trigger is written once as a canonical content-addressed artifact next to the append-only task-attempt ledger",
    "a resumed process verifies the existing trigger artifact and starts zero new queued positions",
    "the incomplete result population continues through the existing Formal Batch verifier and seals HOLD with no Updater or downstream stage"
  ],
